<Vertical id="MermaidPublishDemo" title="Mermaid: live preview vs publish">

<Markdown> Edit the diagram in the editor below. The **live preview**
updates as you type — it reads the editor's value reactively via
`target=`. The **published** diagram only updates when you click
**Publish**, which uses `CopyFieldAction` to write the editor's text
into the published diagram's own value field. </Markdown>

<TextArea id="editor" rows="6">
graph LR
    A[Edit] --> B[Live preview]
    A --> C[Published on click]
</TextArea>

<Markdown>**Live preview** (reactive `target=editor`):</Markdown>
<Mermaid target="editor" />

<Markdown>**Published** (own value field, written by CopyFieldAction):</Markdown>
<Mermaid id="published">
graph LR
    A[Click Publish] --> B[to update this diagram]
</Mermaid>

<ActionButton id="publish_btn" label="Publish"> <CopyFieldAction target="editor" output="published" /> </ActionButton>

<Markdown> **Design note.** Clicking Publish *before* typing in the
editor clears the published diagram, rather than copying over the
placeholder text. This behavior will likely change in the future,
since it's a bit counterintuitive.

Don't rely on it.</Markdown>

</Vertical>
